Chapter: Impression

 An impression is one printing of a work. The first impression and the ninth
 are the same book and different objects, and a colophon that could not tell
 you which one you were holding would be no use to anyone.

 In a content-addressed repository the work has no impressions -- the bytes
 are the bytes, and the same bytes are always the same work, however many
 times they are written down. So an impression here records the ACT of
 printing rather than the thing printed: who did it, and when. That is a fact
 about the world, not about the text, and it is the part the hash cannot
 reach.

Section: Definitions

  Impression = record {
    imp-number : Integer,
    imp-when : Integer,
    imp-printer : Text
  }

  impression-line : Impression -> Text
  impression-line (imp) =
    ordinal (imp.imp-number) & " impression, struck at " & show (imp.imp-when)
    & " by " & (imp.imp-printer)

 Ordinals in English are irregular for exactly three numbers and regular
 forever after, which is the sort of thing a book about books ought to get
 right.

  ordinal : Integer -> Text
  ordinal (n) =
    if n == 1 then "first"
    else if n == 2 then "second"
    else if n == 3 then "third"
    else show n & "th"

